{"name":"Golden Nugget","hex":"#d78e48","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"nugget","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, compact chunk or clump.","A chicken nugget."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To find nuggets (of something valuable)","To smear a male's genitals or anus with boot polish or similar substance against his will."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nugget"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Nugget Hotel & Casinos","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Nugget Hotels & Casinos is an American chain of luxury hotels and casinos. It currently operates eight casino resorts in Colorado, Nevada, Louisiana, New Jersey, Illinois, and Mississippi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6c/Golden_Nugget_Hotel_%26_Casinos_logo.svg/330px-Golden_Nugget_Hotel_%26_Casinos_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Nugget_Hotel_%26_Casinos","wikidata":"Q5579679"},{"title":"Golden Nugget Atlantic City","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Nugget Atlantic City is a hotel, casino, and marina located in Atlantic City, New Jersey, United States. It opened in 1985 as Trump’s Castle and was renamed Trump Marina in 1997. Landry's, Inc. purchased the casino from Trump Entertainment Resorts in February 2011, and the sale was approved in late May. Landry's took control of the property on May 23, 2011, and renamed it the Golden Nugget Atlantic City."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/Logo_Atlantic_city3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Nugget_Atlantic_City","wikidata":"Q3541143"},{"title":"Golden Nugget (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Nugget is a 1996 gambling simulation video game developed by Abalone Entertainment and Software Development, and published by Virgin Interactive Entertainment for Microsoft Windows. A PlayStation version, developed by Point of View, Inc., was also published by Virgin Interactive in 1997. Golden Nugget is set at the Golden Nugget hotel-casino in Las Vegas. It features 16 gambling games, and a story mode that includes a character portrayed by actor Adam West."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Golden_Nugget_game_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Nugget_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q63049670"},{"title":"Gold nugget","blocks":[{"text":"A gold nugget is a naturally occurring piece of native gold. Watercourses often concentrate nuggets and finer gold in placers. Nuggets are recovered by placer mining, but they are also found in residual deposits where the gold-bearing veins or lodes are weathered. Nuggets are also found in the tailings piles of previous mining operations, especially those left by gold mining dredges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Goldinpan.jpg/330px-Goldinpan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_nugget","wikidata":"Q1507004"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Golden_Nugget_LC.JPG/500px-Golden_Nugget_LC.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Golden_Nugget_LC.JPG/1280px-Golden_Nugget_LC.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikime